From: ocean-port <ocean-port@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] OCEAN: let the Xcode 26 iig build xnu-8796

The GitHub macOS runners no longer carry an Xcode old enough to build
xnu-8796.  Xcode 16 and newer ship an "iig" whose generated code
initialises an IORPC with a field this kernel does not have:

    DriverKit/OSObject.iig.cpp:362:133: error: field designator
    'kernelContent' does not refer to any field in type 'IORPC'

The upstream workflow notes the same problem: "macos-14 still ships
Xcode 15.x: its iig matches the xnu-8796 IORPC ABI (Xcode 16's iig
emits IORPC.kernelContent, which this xnu lacks)".  Apple removed the
old Xcode from the hosted images, so the driver has to grow the field
instead.

Xcode's generated code uses it like this:

    .sendSize = sizeof(buf.msg), .replySize = sizeof(buf.rpl),
    .kernelContent = &buf.msg.content.__hdr

so the field is a pointer to the header of the message content, which
is an IORPCMessage.  Adding it to the struct lets the generated code
compile; nothing in this kernel uses the field, because the DriverKit
RPC machinery is not part of the phone build.

There are two copies of IORPC.h in the tree, iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h and
iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h, and both need the field.

Co-Authored-By: ocean-port <ocean-port@example.org>
---
diff --git a/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h b/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h
--- a/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h
+++ b/iokit/DriverKit/IORPC.h
@@ -224,6 +224,19 @@
 	IORPCMessageMach * reply;
 	uint32_t           sendSize;
 	uint32_t           replySize;
+	/*
+	 * Xcode 16 and newer generate an initialiser that names this
+	 * field:
+	 *
+	 *     .sendSize = sizeof(buf.msg), .replySize = sizeof(buf.rpl),
+	 *     .kernelContent = &buf.msg.content.__hdr
+	 *
+	 * The hosted macOS images no longer carry an Xcode old enough to
+	 * build this kernel, so the field has to exist.  It points at the
+	 * header of the message content; nothing in the phone build uses
+	 * it, because the DriverKit RPC machinery is not part of it.
+	 */
+	IORPCMessage      * kernelContent;
 };
 typedef struct IORPC IORPC;
 
diff --git a/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h b/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h
--- a/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h
+++ b/iokit/IOKit/IORPC.h
@@ -224,6 +224,19 @@
 	IORPCMessageMach * reply;
 	uint32_t           sendSize;
 	uint32_t           replySize;
+	/*
+	 * Xcode 16 and newer generate an initialiser that names this
+	 * field:
+	 *
+	 *     .sendSize = sizeof(buf.msg), .replySize = sizeof(buf.rpl),
+	 *     .kernelContent = &buf.msg.content.__hdr
+	 *
+	 * The hosted macOS images no longer carry an Xcode old enough to
+	 * build this kernel, so the field has to exist.  It points at the
+	 * header of the message content; nothing in the phone build uses
+	 * it, because the DriverKit RPC machinery is not part of it.
+	 */
+	IORPCMessage      * kernelContent;
 };
 typedef struct IORPC IORPC;
 
